@vighpeter3 @palhonti1 Thank you so much for the light.

Please note that the correct conversion factor is being applied for compost. We have also learnt that for volume waste submission, we need to first convert volume to mass, then apply the conversion factor (0.5 kg CO₂e per kg).

@vighpeter3  Please note that I am not part of the email threat this was discussed. You can forward me the thread at anytime i will go through it.

@nhlanhlamasuku correct, I believe we have an endpoint already to fetch submitted evidence by ID; however, I am just curious about how well our users can remember the evidence submission ID (either in the form of a UUID or a short code we generate at the system level) :smile:

I will advise that we take a step back and carefully think about the best UX for this. Remember, we already have a preview submission before submission; that step was introduced to eliminate human error, as much as possible.

”Always remember: Recent Activities are nothing but recent submissions”

@nhlanhlamasuku , I would’nt adive to spend time on this; this is by design at the Supabase level.
\- Since we are on the free tier, and if there is no traffic coming to the cluster, they shutdown the cluster
\- Free tier runs on EC2 nano, hence chances are that on high volume traffic, the cluster will be under stress (CPU and RAM) and run out of capacity.
